xpl
---
A udp server that listens for edit commands
over an arbitrary port. The received command
is of format `filename:range` and is sent to
the plumber so that it can be opened by sam/acme.
xpl is to be run on plan9/9front. Of course,
said file is expected to be found under /mnt/term.

Usage
---
% xpl &

You can send a request to said port (default: 11222)
using netcat like this:

$ echo file:1,5 | ncat -u $ip 11222

'e' is a simple utility which does this
for you.

Rationale
---
This tool exists because some of us like to
use the programming environment (sam and rio)
of plan9, although, we can't switch from Linux/BSD
due to other reasons. This tool will help in
such a usecase where you want to navigate a
file tree using your local shell and invoke
'e' on a file to edit using your favorite
plan9 editor.

CAVEATS
---
You can only send `edit` commands i.e. you
can't open a pdf with page or so on plan9.
In short, this is not a generic external plumber.

